# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES R13 — A BACKLINK TITLE RESOLVES ACROSS ORGS
# (ADR-053 §6 R13; WS-Notes Phase 4 unit 4.3 / gate P4). `Samen.Web.Notes.Links.resolve/3`
# stops reading through the acting scope and reads with `authorize?: false`: the candidate
# `Doc` is now ANY org's live page with that title, so org A's `[[Foreign Secret]]` resolves to
# org B's page and a `DocLink` edge is attempted toward a page the reader can never open. The
# second defence (`SameOrgFk` on both link endpoints) still refuses the INSERT, which is why the
# sabotage aims at RESOLUTION: the invariant the gate names is "a cross-org title does not
# resolve", and that is the boundary this patch removes.
#
# Aimed at the lookup only: the tokeniser, the set-reconcile in `Writes.sync_links/3`, the
# archive filtering and every search clause are untouched, so exactly the R13 test flips (the
# positive control — org B resolving its OWN title — still passes, proving the failure is the
# scope, not the fixture).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_search_links_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a cross-org title does NOT resolve (R13) — and the positive control does
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/links.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/links.ex
@@ -64,13 +64,16 @@
       mount
       |> doc_resource()
       |> Ash.Query.ensure_selected([:id, :title])
       |> Ash.Query.filter(title == ^title)
       |> Ash.Query.limit(1)
 
-    case Ash.read(query, scope: scope) do
+    # SABOTAGE (R13): the lookup is unscoped — any org's page with this title resolves.
+    _ = scope
+
+    case Ash.read(query, authorize?: false) do
       {:ok, [doc | _]} -> {:ok, doc}
       _ -> :unresolved
     end
   end
 
   def resolve(_mount, _scope, _title), do: :unresolved
